														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2392838">
									

<p>The problem is this article is trying to do way too much. We have addendums that go on to explain what this universe is, when I thought the most interesting thing about it was that it's this weird, mysterious afterlife that happened to be a 1800s sanitarium. The intro of walking into an alternate reality with hemlock is a great start, filled with mystery, but this wonderful atmosphere is lost by explaining everything. Plus, you're already trying to create an entire dimension, but now you want to create an entire profile of a new GOI on top of that; and then on top of that you're creating a new object class; and then on top of that there's the unnecessary coda with business cards, which did nothing for me.</p>
<p>The article should have ended after -5. Personally, I would keep the stairs and -2 through -5, and remove all the others. They don't fit the narrative you're telling, some of them break tone (article seems to be going for weird, but then there's the Liar Pit which is gruesome, and the cloud which I thought was really funny), and their inclusion in this world that seems to focus on the soul-eating beast and body-eating tiles just bogs the rest down.</p>
<p>I'm not a fan of the format either. Contrast this with something like <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-1165">SCP-1165</a>. To give each weird thing a separate designation makes us regard each thing as separate, and the result is disjointed. Make it all part of the same world and we take in the environment as a whole.</p>
<p>Please rewrite, because there's a good SCP in here. The problem is it's weighed down by too much excess.</p>

							</div>

								
