			<div class="content" id="post-content-2392859">
									

<p>Your new creepy cult is way too reliant on already established creepy cults to stand on it's own. The CotBG is written from plenty of other angles than crazy jerks, Fifthism is too weird to be labeled, and Sarkism is played straight, but with great detail and heavy lore. This Brazen Heart stuff has none of that, so I have no reason to care about them.</p>
<p>As for your new object class, I don't see the point, especially in this context. Why does anything else beyond making sure nobody reaches SCP-2427-A need to be done? The only mobile thing to worry about is SCP-2427-3, and on the chance it did find a sprig of hemlock and left, it would be contained like any other SCP that can't be looked at.</p>
<p>Overall, nothing adds up. I don't know why the foundation would send researchers to a dangerous extradimensional space for no reason, or why these Molok guys have such great taste in interior decorating.</p>

