			<div class="content" id="post-content-2392862">
									

<p>I think what Dave is trying to do with this Moloch/Molok stuff is basically what Meta did with the FLESH and Djoric did with the Scarlet King, with implications tying to both of those.</p>
<p>The writing here isn't incompetent, but it's not compelling. It uses a lot of well-established tropes and doesn't do anything new with them. To list a few, we have 1) an anomalous prophet/demigod/other servant of a god, 2) a place that exists in hammerspace (seriously, the Foundationverse is like, 90℅ hammerspace by volume), 3) a Strange Evil-but-justified-in-their-belief cult/cult that worships a Real Deity, 4) and an Ominous Countdown Timer. Those aren't even everything. These tropes can definitely still work (a lot of my favorites use some of these; <em>I've</em> used some of these) but they're not properly applied. I understand the idea that this is meant to be a sacred place for a religion you've probably mulled over a lot, that this is meant to be part of a larger mythos, but I don't feel like you presented it well. Your afterlife skip and the original Liar's Den are both pretty good at the Bigger Implications thing in my opinion, but this doesn't so much imply as rub our noses in it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
